.\" sermoman-mcp.1 — man page for sermoman-mcp
.\" haplo-dialog <devel@haplo-dialog.fr>
.\" Installed as /usr/share/man/man1/sermoman-mcp.1
.TH SERMOMAN-MCP 1 "October 2026" "sermo @PACKAGE_VERSION@" "sermo User Commands"
.SH NAME
sermoman-mcp \- read-only MCP server that gives an AI assistant the sermo manual
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sermoman-mcp
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sermoman-mcp
is a Model Context Protocol server. It speaks JSON-RPC on its standard input and
output and is started by an MCP client (an AI assistant), not by hand. It only
reads its own documentation: it runs no command and writes no file.
.PP
Its tools:
.BR sermo_reference ,
.BR sermo_guide ,
.BR sermo_architecture ,
.BR sermo_heritage ,
.BR sermo_ecosystem ,
.B sermo_scripts
(the job scripts and toolboxes),
.BR sermo_search ,
.B sermo_example
and
.BR sermo_how_to_report .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/sermoman-mcp/data
the documentation it serves.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
claude mcp add sermoman -- /usr/bin/sermoman-mcp
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sermo (1),
.BR sermoia-mcp (1),
.I /usr/share/doc/sermoman-mcp/README.md
.SH AUTHOR
haplo-dialog <devel@haplo-dialog.fr>
